Ladybird keeps a table’s original display on its table wrapper, the box
that gets positioned, so an absolutely positioned table that was block-
level gets its static position at the start of its containing block,
whatever the text-align, and Blink, WebKit and Gecko all place it there.
Gecko’s wrapper frame inherits the table’s display, and ReflowInput::
CalculateHypotheticalPosition() checks IsOriginalDisplayInlineOutside()
on it. Blink records IsOriginalDisplayInlineType() before adjusting the
display, and its InlineLayoutAlgorithm::PlaceOutOfFlowObjects() reads
that. And WebKit’s InlineDisplayContentBuilder classifies the box with
style().originalDisplay().isInlineType().
